WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:14.266
daybreak I woke up to a series of awful screams from Bill.

2
00:00:15.186 --> 00:00:20.550
They weren't yells, howls, shouts, whoops, or yelps, like you'd expect from a man's vocal cords.

3
00:00:21.611 --> 00:00:28.676
Instead they were simply shameless, terrifying, humiliating screams, like when women see a ghost or a caterpillar.

4
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:35.736
It's an awful thing to hear a strong, desperate, fat man shrieking uncontrollably in a cave at daybreak.

5
00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:40.619
I jumped up to see what was wrong and saw Red Chief sitting on Bill's chest.

6
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.843
One of the boy's hands held a hank of Bill's hair while the other hand waved the sharp

7
00:00:45.943 --> 00:00:47.604
knife we'd used for slicing bacon.

8
00:00:48.405 --> 00:00:51.467
Red Chief was about to give Bill a very bad haircut.

9
00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:54.208
I pried the knife out of the kid's fingers.

10
00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:55.629
"Stop it!

11
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:56.930
Leave Bill alone!

12
00:00:57.331 --> 00:00:58.811
Lie down and stay down!"

13
00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.292
I yelled.

14
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.841
But from that moment, Bill's spirit was broken.

15
00:01:03.702 --> 00:01:07.664
He lay down on his side of the bed, and never closed an eye again in sleep as

16
00:01:07.784 --> 00:01:09.185
long as that boy was with us.

17
00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:14.328
I dozed off for a while, but I remembered later that Red Chief had said I was to

18
00:01:14.368 --> 00:01:16.709
be burned at the stake at the rising of the sun.

19
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:22.893
I wasn't nervous or afraid, but I sat up, lit my pipe, and leaned against a rock.

20
00:01:22.913 --> 00:01:25.514
"Why are you getting up so soon, Sam?"

21
00:01:25.775 --> 00:01:26.295
asked Bill.

22
00:01:26.315 --> 00:01:27.916
"Me?" I said.

23
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.522
"Oh, I got a little pain in my shoulder.

24
00:01:30.942 --> 00:01:32.823
I thought sitting up would make it feel better."

25
00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:34.424
"You're a liar!"

26
00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:35.085
said Bill.

27
00:01:35.445 --> 00:01:38.547
"You're supposed to be burned at sunrise, and you're afraid he'll do it.

28
00:01:39.388 --> 00:01:41.389
And he would too, if he could find a match.

29
00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:43.191
This is awful, Sam.

30
00:01:43.711 --> 00:01:47.414
Do you think anyone will pay good money to get a rotten kid like that back?"

31
00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.575
"Sure," I said.

32
00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:52.918
"A wild kid like that is just the kind that parents spoil.

33
00:01:53.778 --> 00:01:56.060
Now you and the chief get up and cook breakfast.

34
00:01:56.608 --> 00:01:59.471
I'll go up on top of this mountain and see if anything is happening."

35
00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:03.574
I hiked over to the peak of the little mountain and looked toward the horizon.

36
00:02:04.415 --> 00:02:09.440
When I spied the town of Summit, I expected to see packs of villagers armed with axes and

37
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.343
pitchforks running around the countryside searching for the dastardly kidnappers.

38
00:02:14.284 --> 00:02:19.669
But what I saw was a peaceful landscape and one man plowing a field with a grayish-brown mule.

39
00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.792
Nobody was searching the creek for a drowned child.

40
00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.622
No messengers ran here and there bringing news of no news to the worried parents.

41
00:02:28.642 --> 00:02:34.044
Everything I could see from the top of that mountain looked calm and drowsy, if not already asleep.

42
00:02:34.064 --> 00:02:40.707
"Perhaps they haven't yet discovered that the wolves have stolen away their tender little lamb," I said to

43
00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.948
myself. Then I swallowed and thought of Red Chief.

44
00:02:44.749 --> 00:02:46.389
"Heaven help the wolves!"

45
00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.011
I yelled to the serene valley and went down the mountain to breakfast.

46
00:02:50.991 --> 00:02:55.170
When I got back to the hideout, I found Bill with his back up against the wall of

47
00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:55.670
the cave.

48
00:02:56.571 --> 00:02:57.631
He was breathing hard.

49
00:02:57.992 --> 00:03:02.214
The boy was holding a coconut-sized rock in both hands and was shaking it at him.

50
00:03:02.235 --> 00:03:04.476
"I'll smash you with this!"

51
00:03:04.676 --> 00:03:05.557
Red Chief shouted.

52
00:03:06.377 --> 00:03:08.599
Bill saw me and started talking fast.

53
00:03:08.619 --> 00:03:12.561
"He dropped a red-hot boiled potato down my back.

54
00:03:13.422 --> 00:03:14.983
Then he mashed it with his foot!

55
00:03:15.584 --> 00:03:17.185
It hurt so much, I slapped him.

56
00:03:17.925 --> 00:03:19.366
Have you got your gun, Sam?"

57
00:03:20.407 --> 00:03:21.928
I grabbed the rock away from the boy.

58
00:03:22.412 --> 00:03:24.053
"Come on, now, you two," I said.

59
00:03:24.073 --> 00:03:24.994
"Play nice."

60
00:03:25.014 --> 00:03:28.016
"I'll fix you," the kid told Bill.

61
00:03:28.036 --> 00:03:31.238
"No man ever struck Red Chief and got away with it.

62
00:03:31.618 --> 00:03:32.698
You'll be sorry!"

63
00:03:33.619 --> 00:03:37.982
After breakfast, the kid took a piece of leather with strings wrapped around it out of his pocket.

64
00:03:38.662 --> 00:03:41.204
He went outside the cave and started to unwind it.

65
00:03:42.064 --> 00:03:43.145
"What's he up to now?"

66
00:03:43.345 --> 00:03:44.726
asked Bill in a scared voice.

67
00:03:44.746 --> 00:03:47.668
"You don't think he'll run away, do you, Sam?"

68
00:03:48.524 --> 00:03:52.565
When he asked me this, Bill sounded hopeful as he pressed his hands together in a kind of

69
00:03:52.685 --> 00:03:54.806
prayer. "Nope," I said.

70
00:03:54.826 --> 00:03:56.607
"He's not much of a homebody.

71
00:03:57.007 --> 00:03:59.728
We've got to think up some plan about the ransom.

72
00:04:00.728 --> 00:04:06.450
There's no excitement around Summit about the boy's disappearance, but maybe they haven't realized that he's gone yet.

73
00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:10.831
His folks may think he's spending the night with an aunt or one of his neighbors.

74
00:04:11.691 --> 00:04:13.112
Anyhow he'll be missed today.

75
00:04:14.004 --> 00:04:18.966
Tonight we've got to get a message to his father demanding the two thousand dollars for his return."

76
00:04:19.846 --> 00:04:24.527
Just then we heard a different kind of war whoop, like David might have shouted when he knocked

77
00:04:24.587 --> 00:04:26.168
out Goliath in ancient times.

78
00:04:27.048 --> 00:04:31.190
"OOOUUU-WOWWW!" "He's got a sling!"

79
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:31.670
I yelled.

80
00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.350
"Look out!"

81
00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:38.652
Red Chief started whirling the weapon around his head, and I ducked in time, but Bill didn't.

82
00:04:39.584 --> 00:04:43.846
Then I heard a heavy thud, and Bill screamed like he'd been shot through the head with an

83
00:04:43.966 --> 00:04:50.068
arrow. A smooth black rock the size of an egg had caught Bill just behind his left ear.

84
00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:56.231
He wobbled, lost his balance, and then fell across the pan of hot water on the fire that

85
00:04:56.251 --> 00:04:57.832
had been used for washing the dishes.

86
00:04:58.872 --> 00:05:02.373
I dragged him out and poured cool water on his head for half an hour.

87
00:05:03.314 --> 00:05:06.235
Finally Bill sat up and felt behind his ear.

88
00:05:07.115 --> 00:05:11.657
He asked, "Sam, did you ever learn the Ten Commandments when you were a kid?"

89
00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:14.338
"Yeah, sure," I said.

90
00:05:14.358 --> 00:05:16.459
"Do you remember the sixth one?"

91
00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:17.240
he asked.

92
00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.021
I took a wild guess.

93
00:05:19.641 --> 00:05:20.561
"Do not kill?"

94
00:05:20.581 --> 00:05:23.482
"I thought of an exception," Bill said.

95
00:05:23.502 --> 00:05:26.024
"You'll feel better soon," I said.

96
00:05:26.824 --> 00:05:27.904
Bill grabbed my hand.

97
00:05:27.924 --> 00:05:31.026
"You won't go away and leave me here alone, will you, Sam?"

98
00:05:31.766 --> 00:05:35.888
I went out and caught that boy and shook him until his freckles rattled.
